Subject: calling setContentType outside of an R handler
Message-ID: <uEIMxsws43o.bSnNCZ7T4pYJ@rapache.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rapache/c/uEIMxsws43o/m/bSnNCZ7T4pYJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello Rapache folks -

I'm attempting to make calls to the function setContentType outside
the file that RFileHandler directive point to.

This works:

## helloworld.R
main <- function() {
  setContentType("text/html")
  cat("<html><body><h1> Hello world </h1></body></html>")
}

But calling setContentType from a sourced file doesn't work:

## helloworld2.R
main <- function() {
  sys.source("setContentType.R")
 cat("<html><body><h1> Hello world </h1></body></html>")
}

## file setContentType.R
setContentType("text/html")

The error is:  could not find function "setContentType"

----
What's the appropriate way to call setContentType, sendBin, and other
rapache-specific commands from files outside the RHandler?

Here's the relevant apache2.conf snippet:

<Location "/helloworld">
 ROutputErrors
 Options indexes FollowSymLinks
 SetHandler r-handler
 RFileHandler /var/www/R/helloworld.R::main
</Location>

Thanks!

From u25a4f5811cd7d59e at groups.google.com  Mon Jan 25 13:52:54 2010
From: u25a4f5811cd7d59e at groups.google.com (Jeffrey Horner)
Date: Mon, 25 Jan 2010 13:52:54 +0000
Subject: Re: calling setContentType outside of an R handler
Message-ID: <uEIMxsws43o.8LYS1i4mu8wJ@rapache.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <uEIMxsws43o.bSnNCZ7T4pYJ@rapache.groups.google.com>
References: <uEIMxsws43o.bSnNCZ7T4pYJ@rapache.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rapache/c/uEIMxsws43o/m/8LYS1i4mu8wJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You'll want to call sys.source with the argument envir=sys.frame(sys.nframe()).
Otherwise sys.source() evaluates the file in the base environment.

An alternative way would be calling source() with local=TRUE.

Jeff

